  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "Education is the structured or informal process of transmitting knowledge, skills, and character traits, aimed at empowering individuals and fostering personal, social, and economic development. It spans early childhood to tertiary levels, emphasizing critical thinking, skill mastery, and lifelong learning to promote equality and economic mobility. Key Aspects of Education: Types of Education: Formal Education: Structured schooling systems (schools, universities). Non-formal Education: Structured but outside the formal system, such as vocational training. Informal Education: Unstructured learning through daily experiences. Levels of Education: Early Childhood/Pre-primary: Foundational care and education. Primary Education: Basic literacy and numeracy. Secondary Education: Furthering academic and life skills. Tertiary/Higher Education: Universities, vocational, and technical training. Benefits of Education: Individual Empowerment: Cultivates critical thinking, character, and potential. Socioeconomic Mobility: Provides paths out of poverty and increases employability. Social Development: Promotes equality, gender parity, and peace. Importance & Goals of Education: Core Purpose: To foster intellectual growth, technical skills, and personal fulfillment. Global Goals: Achieve universal primary/secondary education, promote lifelong learning, and ensure safe, inclusive learning environments. Four Pillars: Learning to know, to do, to live together, and to be. Philosophy & Approaches: Modern education increasingly focuses on learner-centered approaches like Montessori, while prioritizing digital and transferable skills for a changing world. Organizations like the National Education Association (NEA) and UNESCO emphasize protecting the right to quality, inclusive education.",
